-- Fixed 2026-09-20: ASSET_AMT/INCOME_AMT/REVENUE_AMT were bare try_to_double()
-- calls. Live-checked (this table is only 2,450 rows -- the check covers all
-- of it, not a sample): 0 fractional values in any of the three columns
-- today, so no active rounding bug, but still an unguarded landmine against
-- 'nan' strings and any future decimal load. Now reads the already-guarded
-- staging model (same 28 columns, same order): the staging generator profiled
-- these three as whole-number and casts them with stg_int, which matches what
-- the live data actually is; a future non-whole value goes NULL instead of
-- being silently accepted or poisoned by a stray 'nan'. Six more columns
-- (affiliation, classification, deductibility, tax_period, asset_cd,
-- income_cd, pf_filing_req_cd) pick up the same stg_int guard as a bonus --
-- they were uncast text in the mart before.

